# Quant Stock Momentum Research Pro v5

A stock-only quantitative research/backtesting system for U.S. equities. It is designed for research and paper signal generation only; it does **not** send live orders.

v5 builds on the previous adaptive total-return engine and adds a more robust broad-market participation sleeve, extra signal features, expanded universe support, and out-of-sample config selection.

## What changed in v5

- Added `adaptive_total_return_v5` portfolio mode.
- Added 1/N-inspired broad sleeve with optional mild quality/momentum tilt.
- Added new signal components:
  - volatility-adjusted 12-1 momentum,
  - Kaufman-style efficiency/smooth trend ratio,
  - persistence near 52-week highs,
  - existing residual, intermediate, breakout, trend, downside-quality, and volatility-contraction signals.
- Expanded default universe from about 62 symbols to 111 stocks plus SPY benchmark.
- Added config variants:
  - `configs/strategy_balanced.yml`
  - `configs/strategy_growth.yml`
  - `configs/strategy_sharpe.yml`
  - `configs/strategy_equal_weight_plus.yml`
- Added `scripts/run_oos_config_selection.py` for train/validation/test config selection.
- Updated the strategy suite and parameter-sensitivity scripts to include v5 variants.

## Setup

```cmd
cd quant_stock_momentum_research_pro_v5
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -e .
```

## Recommended data source: yfinance adjusted stock data

```cmd
python scripts/download_yfinance_stocks.py --instruments configs/instruments.yml --data-dir data/raw/yfinance --start 2014-01-01 --end 2026-01-01 --include-benchmark --skip-failed
```

The expanded universe has more symbols, so use `--skip-failed` to avoid one failed ticker stopping the entire download.

## Dukascopy alternative

```cmd
python scripts/download_dukascopy_stocks.py --instruments configs/instruments.yml --data-dir data/raw/dukascopy --start 2018-01-01 --end 2026-01-01 --timeframe d1 --include-benchmark --skip-failed
```

Dukascopy stock CFDs may have zero or unreliable volume. The code handles this, but adjusted equity data is still better for stock research.

## Diagnose data

```cmd
python scripts/diagnose_data.py --data-dir data/raw/yfinance --instruments configs/instruments.yml --out data/reports/data_quality.csv --allow-missing
```

## Run the v5 default backtest

```cmd
python scripts/run_backtest.py --data-dir data/raw/yfinance --instruments configs/instruments.yml --strategy configs/strategy.yml --out data/reports/pro_v5_default --allow-missing
```

## Compare all strategy variants

```cmd
python scripts/run_strategy_suite.py --data-dir data/raw/yfinance --instruments configs/instruments.yml --out data/reports/strategy_suite_v5 --allow-missing
```

Review:

```text
data/reports/strategy_suite_v5/strategy_suite_summary.csv
```

## Walk-forward validation

```cmd
python scripts/run_walk_forward.py --data-dir data/raw/yfinance --instruments configs/instruments.yml --strategy configs/strategy.yml --out data/reports/walk_forward_v5 --allow-missing
```

## Out-of-sample config selection

This script compares the predefined v3/v4/v5 configs, selects using validation-period robust score, then reports test-period and full-period results.

```cmd
python scripts/run_oos_config_selection.py --data-dir data/raw/yfinance --instruments configs/instruments.yml --out data/reports/oos_config_selection_v5 --allow-missing
```

Default split:

```text
train:       2014-01-01 to 2018-12-31
validation:  2019-01-01 to 2021-12-31
test:        2022-01-01 onward
```

## Cost stress

```cmd
python scripts/run_cost_stress.py --data-dir data/raw/yfinance --instruments configs/instruments.yml --strategy configs/strategy.yml --out data/reports/cost_stress_v5 --allow-missing
```

